    "pr_title": "variable, main: make sure default values for sysvars validate",
    "pr_body": "### What problem does this PR solve?\r\n\r\nProblem Summary:\r\n\r\nFixes https://github.com/pingcap/tidb/issues/24794 \r\n\r\nThis adds a new test to the variable package, and fixes a few inconsistencies.\r\n\r\nIf you try and set a sysvar to its default value, it should both pass validation and the value should already be normalized.\r\n\r\nThis is incredibly useful, because the most annoying thing is trying to set a setting to something like what it already is, but it fails validation.\r\n\r\nThis also increases the code-coverage for variable:\r\n```\r\nFrom:\r\nok  \tgithub.com/pingcap/tidb/sessionctx/variable\t0.012s\tcoverage: 48.7% of statements\r\nTo:\r\nok  \tgithub.com/pingcap/tidb/sessionctx/variable\t0.014s\tcoverage: 52.7% of statements\r\n```\r\n\r\n### What is changed and how it works?\r\n\r\nWhat's Changed:\r\n\r\nAdded test and inconsistencies fixed.\r\n\r\n### Related changes\r\n\r\n- None\r\n\r\n### Check List <!--REMOVE the items that are not applicable-->\r\n\r\nTests <!-- At least one of them must be included. -->\r\n\r\n- Unit test\r\n\r\nSide effects\r\n\r\n- None\r\n\r\n### Release note <!-- bugfixes or new feature need a release note -->\r\n\r\n- No release note",
